  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1013 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nThe cool temperatures will continue into Monday as the low stratus \nlayer is expected to prevail. Highs in the upper 40s to lower 50s \nare expected across the area. We will see a small break in the fog \nlater Sunday and overnight, however patchy fog will be possible \nagain early Monday morning for the far southwestern Texas Panhandle \nand portions of the South Plains. Some localized areas could see \ndense fog as well. A slight warm up will begin Tuesday as upper \nridging will fill in overhead with highs expected to return to the \n60s by mid-week. This upper pattern change will also dry out \nconditions through much of the work week. Precipitation chances may \nreturn the following weekend. Models indicate the upper ridging will \npush east as an upper shortwave swings across the Rockies. Shower \nand thunderstorm chances will be dependent on the track of the upper \nshortwave. If the shortwave passes to the north, we could get dry \nslotted. As we get closer through the week, models should better \nalign with the upper pattern.",
